# UCITS eligibility screen: the diversification rules of the UCITS Directive
# (2009/65/EC, articles 52 and 55), as a what-if on the account. Would the
# account qualify as a UCITS fund as it stands?
#
# Article 52 limits "transferable securities and money market instruments" of one
# body - shares and bonds alike. Securities issued or guaranteed by a state are
# under 52(3) instead, and by 52(5) do not count towards the 40% of 52(2).
# Version 1 cited 52(4) for the government limit (52(4) is covered bonds) and
# applied the issuer limits to shares only.

mandate "UCITS eligibility screen" version 2 effective 2024-04-04

rule issuer_10 "No issuer above 10% (art. 52(1), raised by 52(2))" hard
    max weight by issuer where asset_class in ("equity", "fixed income") and issuer_type = "corporate" <= 10%

rule five_ten_forty "Issuers above 5% together at most 40% (art. 52(2); state issues excluded, 52(5))" hard
    sum weight by issuer above 5% where asset_class in ("equity", "fixed income") and issuer_type = "corporate" <= 40%

rule government_35 "Any one state issuer at most 35% (art. 52(3))" hard
    max weight by issuer where issuer_type = "government" <= 35%

rule fund_20 "Any one fund at most 20% (art. 55(1), where national law raises its 10%)" hard
    max weight by instrument where asset_class = "fund" <= 20%
